    <!-- Phantom Process Killer Section -->
    <section class="ppk" id="ppk">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Phantom <span class="gradient-text">Process Killer</span></h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Termux may be unstable on Android 12+ — here's how to fix it</p>
            </div>
            <div class="notice-box">
                <div class="notice-icon">ℹ️</div>
                <div class="notice-content">
                    <h4>Notice</h4>
                    <p>Android OS will kill any phantom processes greater than 32 (limit is for all apps combined) and
                        also kill any processes using excessive CPU. You may get
                        <code>[Process completed (signal 9) - press Enter]</code> in the terminal without exiting the
                        shell yourself. Check the
                        <a href="https://github.com/termux/termux-app/issues/2366" target="_blank" rel="noopener">related
                            issue</a> and
                        <a href="https://gist.github.com/agnostic-apollo/dc7e47991c512755ff26bd2d31e72ca8" target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener">this gist</a>
                        for more details.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ppk-grid">
                <div class="ppk-card">
                    <div class="ppk-icon adb">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2" />
                            <path d="M8 9h.01M16 9h.01M9 15h6" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Deactivate via ADB</h3>
                    <p>Paste the following commands on an ADB console, in order:</p>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>adb shell "/system/bin/device_config set_sync_disabled_for_tests persistent"</code></pre>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>adb shell "/system/bin/device_config put activity_manager max_phantom_processes 2147483647"</code></pre>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>adb shell settings put global settings_enable_monitor_phantom_procs false</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="ppk-card">
                    <div class="ppk-icon root">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path d="M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5z" />
                            <path d="M2 17l10 5 10-5" />
                            <path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Deactivate via ROOT</h3>
                    <p>On Termux (or any terminal emulator), paste the following commands in order:</p>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>su -c /system/bin/device_config set_sync_disabled_for_tests persistent</code></pre>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>su -c /system/bin/device_config put activity_manager max_phantom_processes 2147483647</code></pre>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>su -c setprop persist.sys.fflag.override.settings_enable_monitor_phantom_procs false</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="ppk-card">
                    <div class="ppk-icon magisk">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path d="M3 12a9 9 0 0118 0" />
                            <path d="M3 12a9 9 0 0018 0" />
                            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Experimental Method (MAGISK)</h3>
                    <p>On a rooted phone with Magisk installed, flash the following module:</p>
                    <a class="btn btn-outline btn-sm"
                        href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HardcodedCat/termux-monet/master/ppr/PhantomProcessRetainer-main.zip"
                        target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                        LetTheGhostsOut.zip
                    </a>
                    <p class="ppk-note">After that, the Phantom Process Killer might be deactivated on every device
                        boot. Please make an <a href="https://github.com/Termux-Monet/termux-monet/issues"
                            target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue</a> if the module didn't work for you.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="ppk-card">
                    <div class="ppk-icon verify">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
                            <path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Verify it was Disabled (ROOT)</h3>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>su -c /system/bin/dumpsys activity settings | grep max_phantom_processes</code></pre>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>su -c /system/bin/device_config get activity_manager max_phantom_processes</code></pre>
                    <p class="ppk-note">Both commands above should return <code>2147483647</code>.</p>
                    <pre class="code-block"><code>su -c getprop persist.sys.fflag.override.settings_enable_monitor_phantom_procs</code></pre>
                    <p class="ppk-note">It should return <code>false</code>.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Debugging Section -->
    <section class="debugging" id="debugging">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Debugging &amp; <span class="gradient-text">Log Levels</span></h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Help debug problems of the Termux app and its plugins</p>
            </div>
            <div class="debug-content">
                <p class="debug-text">
                    Set an appropriate <code>logcat</code> <strong>Log Level</strong> in
                    <em>Termux app settings → &lt;APP_NAME&gt; → Debugging → Log Level</em>
                    (requires Termux app version <code>&gt;= 0.118.0</code>). It defaults to <strong>Normal</strong> and
                    level <strong>Verbose</strong> logs additional information. Revert to <strong>Normal</strong> after
                    debugging since private data may otherwise be passed to <code>logcat</code>.
                </p>
                <div class="log-levels">
                    <span class="log-level">Off</span>
                    <span class="log-level active">Normal</span>
                    <span class="log-level">Debug</span>
                    <span class="log-level">Verbose</span>
                </div>
                <p class="debug-text">
                    Plugin apps don't execute the commands themselves — they send intents to Termux, so set the log
                    level for both Termux and each plugin. Once set, run <code>logcat</code> in the Termux terminal to
                    view logs in realtime (<code>Ctrl+c</code> to stop) or dump them to a file:
                </p>
                <pre class="code-block"><code>logcat</code></pre>
                <pre class="code-block"><code>logcat -d > logcat.txt</code></pre>
                <p class="debug-text">
                    You can also generate <code>stat</code> info and a <code>logcat</code> dump automatically via the
                    terminal's long hold options menu → <strong>More</strong> → <strong>Report Issue</strong>. Users
                    must post complete reports (optionally without sensitive info) — issues opened with partial
                    screenshots instead of text will likely be closed.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Forking Section -->
    <section class="forking" id="forking">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Forking <span class="gradient-text">Instructions</span></h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Want to build your own Termux-Monet based app?</p>
            </div>
            <div class="forking-list">
                <div class="forking-item">
                    <span class="forking-num">1</span>
                    <p>Check <a href="https://github.com/Termux-Monet/termux-monet/blob/master/termux-shared/src/main/java/com/termux/shared/termux/TermuxConstants.java"
                            target="_blank" rel="noopener">TermuxConstants</a> javadocs for instructions on what changes
                        to make to change the package name.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="forking-item">
                    <span class="forking-num">2</span>
                    <p>Keep <code>targetSdk 28</code> to avoid the login error <code>not exec("/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/login"): Permission denied</code>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="forking-item">
                    <span class="forking-num">3</span>
                    <p>Recompile the <a href="https://github.com/termux/termux-packages/wiki/For-maintainers#build-bootstrap-archives"
                            target="_blank" rel="noopener">bootstrap zip</a> for the new package name.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="forking-item">
                    <span class="forking-num">4</span>
                    <p>Not all plugins use <code>TermuxConstants</code> yet — some have hardcoded <code>com.termux</code>
                        values and need manual patching.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="forking-item">
                    <span class="forking-num">5</span>
                    <p>Enable GitHub Actions and do any commit (e.g. upload a placeholder file) to build the app. Create
                        empty releases — GitHub Actions uploads the APKs automatically.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Download Section -->
    <section class="download" id="download">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Get <span class="gradient-text">Termux-Monet</span></h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Download from your preferred source</p>
            </div>
            <div class="download-grid">
                <a href="https://github.com/Termux-Monet/termux-monet/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                    class="download-card primary">
                    <div class="download-info">
                        <h3>GitHub Releases</h3>
                        <p>Stabler releases — APKs under the release assets</p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="download-arrow">→</span>
                </a>
                <a href="https://github.com/Termux-Monet/termux-monet/actions/workflows/debug_build.yml" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener" class="download-card">
                    <div class="download-info">
                        <h3>GitHub Actions</h3>
                        <p>Latest unstable nightly builds — APKs under the artifacts</p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="download-arrow">→</span>
                </a>
                <a href="https://github.com/Termux-Monet/termux-monet" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                    class="download-card">
                    <div class="download-info">
                        <h3>Source Code</h3>
                        <p>Build it yourself from the repository</p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="download-arrow">→</span>
                </a>
            </div>
            <div class="warning-box">
                <div class="warning-icon">🔐</div>
                <div class="warning-content">
                    <h4>Security Warning</h4>
                    <p>APK files on GitHub are signed with a <a
                            href="https://github.com/termux/termux-app/blob/master/app/testkey_untrusted.jks"
                            target="_blank" rel="noopener">test key shared with the community</a>. This is not an
                        official developer key and everyone can use it to forge a malicious Termux update installable
                        over the GitHub build. Think twice before installing Termux builds distributed via Telegram or
                        other social media — this key is easy to detect in user generated content.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Resources Section -->
    <section class="community" id="resources">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">More Info &amp; <span class="gradient-text">Resources</span></h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Learn Termux inside and out</p>
            </div>
            <div class="community-grid">
                <a href="https://github.com/Termux-Monet/termux-monet" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                    class="community-card github">
                    <div class="community-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
                            <path
                                d="M12 0C5.37 0 0 5.37 0 12c0 5.31 3.435 9.795 8.205 11.385.6.105.825-.255.825-.57 0-.285-.015-1.23-.015-2.235-3.015.555-3.795-.735-4.035-1.41-.135-.345-.72-1.41-1.23-1.695-.42-.225-1.02-.78-.015-.795.945-.015 1.62.87 1.845 1.23 1.08 1.815 2.805 1.305 3.495.99.105-.78.42-1.305.765-1.605-2.67-.3-5.46-1.335-5.46-5.925 0-1.305.465-2.385 1.23-3.225-.12-.3-.54-1.53.12-3.18 0 0 1.005-.315 3.3 1.23.96-.27 1.98-.405 3-.405s2.04.135 3 .405c2.295-1.56 3.3-1.23 3.3-1.23.66 1.65.24 2.88.12 3.18.765.84 1.23 1.905 1.23 3.225 0 4.605-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.925.435.375.81 1.095.81 2.22 0 1.605-.015 2.895-.015 3.3 0 .315.225.69.825.57A12.02 12.02 0 0024 12c0-6.63-5.37-12-12-12z" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>GitHub Repository</h3>
                    <p>Report issues, suggest features or submit pull requests</p>
                </a>
                <a href="https://wiki.termux.dev/wiki/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="community-card wiki">
                    <div class="community-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 014 4v14a3 3 0 00-3-3H2z" />
                            <path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 00-4 4v14a3 3 0 013-3h7z" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Termux Wiki</h3>
                    <p>Package management, remote access, backups and more</p>
                </a>
                <a href="https://github.com/termux/termux-app/wiki" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                    class="community-card appwiki">
                    <div class="community-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <rect x="5" y="2" width="14" height="20" rx="2" ry="2" />
                            <line x1="12" y1="18" x2="12.01" y2="18" />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Termux App Wiki</h3>
                    <p>RUN_COMMAND intent, Android 10 notes and app internals</p>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

